id: pm-rl-bi4v
title: Keep the HTTP receipt crash drill within its unchanged timeout
description: "The existing SIGKILL-at-every-HTTP-to-PM-boundary integration case exceeded its unchanged 300-second timeout during full instrumented release validation. Compare the same case against the main baseline, identify startup, I/O or ownership waits, and preserve every crash boundary and assertion while bringing execution inside the bound."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rl#107"
created_at: "2026-10-15T22:41:40.256Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-03T05:33:12.911Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-03T05:32:47.291Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-03T05:27:11.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: A baseline/candidate timing reproduction identifies the cause; the real eight-boundary drill and complete release gates pass with the existing 300-second timeout and unchanged coverage thresholds.
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T22:50:30.933Z",codex-agent,"Diagnostic baseline: an isolated origin/main source archive, using the same pinned dependencies, passed node --test --test-concurrency=1 --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=*.ts --test-coverage-include=scripts/*.ts --test-name-pattern=\"SIGKILL at every HTTP-to-PM\" test/decision-recovery.test.ts in 276105.853 ms (1/1). The candidate full release run reached the unchanged 300000 ms timeout. This establishes a narrow baseline timing margin; it does not by itself attribute the full-run failure. Keep all eight boundaries and the original timeout. A complete passing candidate gate is still required."
  "2026-10-15T22:55:58.563Z",codex-agent,"The eight crash scenarios use independent trackers and synthetic servers. Run the training/held-out pair concurrently for each of the four boundaries, with at most two scenarios active. Keep every real SIGKILL, replay, physical-request, token, identity and idempotency assertion and the original 300000 ms timeout. This changes scheduling only and avoids eight serial setup/replay intervals consuming the whole wall allowance. Verify the focused case under coverage, then require complete npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-15T23:01:06.478Z",codex-agent,"The bounded pair schedule passed all eight real boundary scenarios under coverage in 254328.583 ms (1/1 test, zero skips). The isolated serial main-source diagnostic measured 276105.853 ms; the earlier serial full candidate hit 300000 ms. These are shared-host observations, not a controlled speedup claim. The diff changes only outer loop order and Promise.all of two independent metric cases; every assertion and the 300000 ms timeout remain."
  "2026-10-15T23:04:28.665Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked verification passed: pm test pm-rl-bi4v --run --progress executed the unchanged 300000 ms inner test successfully in 156944.936 ms, 1/1 with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. The outer harness permits 360 seconds for startup/reporting; the test deadline remains 300 seconds. All eight real crash scenarios retain their original assertions. Full release checks will verify the final schedule with all source coverage thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-16T00:02:53.011Z",codex-agent,"Both full covered runs on 4676320 still hit the original 300-second HTTP crash-test deadline under concurrent validation. Inspection found that fork inherited the parent coverage execArgv and raw V8 output directory and ran from the code checkout. SIGKILL-able built-code children now receive empty execArgv, no raw coverage directory and the actual scratch project cwd. Each child reports a boolean bootstrap observation, and the existing crash test requires it to be uninstrumented. The parent still executes and covers the authored source APIs; no source exclusion, threshold or deadline changes. All eight real crash/accounting scenarios remain."
  "2026-10-16T00:09:31.940Z",codex-agent,"Focused verification with an explicit raw V8 parent directory passed all eight boundaries in 137862.796 ms (1/1, zero skips). Behavioural guard-removal proof in an isolated source snapshot: remove only empty execArgv and NODE_V8_COVERAGE suppression from launch, retain the new child observation and all assertions, then run the covered case; it fails 0/1 in 8975.060 ms with SIGKILL controller inherited V8 coverage. Restoring isolation passes 1/1. This changes neither source coverage scope nor test deadlines; built child dist code is not one of the gated TypeScript sources, and parent source APIs remain exercised."
  "2026-10-16T00:15:13.400Z",codex-agent,"Latest PM-linked verification passes 1/1 with all eight boundaries, zero skips: case 206859.047 ms inside the unchanged 300000 ms test deadline. The full-gate child inheritance regression is explicitly checked at bootstrap; guard removal fails and restored isolation passes. The child also runs with the actual scratch project cwd. No authored source is excluded from coverage, and no test assertion or deadline was removed."
  "2026-10-16T03:47:19.355Z",codex-agent,"Final verification: both complete npm and Bun release gates pass 590/590, zero skips, all four coverage dimensions 100%. All eight real HTTP crash boundaries pass within the unchanged 300-second test limit. Independent datasets execute in bounded pairs; SIGKILL children report and enforce coverage isolation; the parent still covers the complete source inventory. Removing child coverage isolation fails the runtime regression, restored execution passes. No assertion, deadline or threshold was weakened. Leave open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-18T03:01:13.159Z",codex-agent,"Audit: MET against recorded acceptance in merged PR #80. The serial baseline measured 276105.853 ms; concurrent full runs hit the unchanged 300000 ms limit. Forked crash children inherited V8 coverage; isolated child execArgv and raw coverage output plus bounded independent pairs retain all eight real HTTP-to-PM crash boundaries. Guard-only revert fails with inherited-coverage evidence; restored focused and linked runs pass. Both full release gates passed 590/590 with all eight boundaries within 300000 ms and unchanged four-metric thresholds. No remaining acceptance gap in that evidence; leave open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-26T21:32:01.185Z",codex-agent,"Reobserved in both complete toolchain candidate gates: the unchanged SIGKILL-at-every-HTTP-to-PM-boundary test reached the 300000 ms deadline under concurrent shared load. npm reported 300000.3143 ms and Bun 300012.0205 ms. This does not attribute a source regression; the originally failing lineage fixtures pass independently. Reopen this existing timing item instead of creating a duplicate. Preserve all eight crash boundaries, the timeout and all coverage thresholds. The complete gates are still running, so no full pass is claimed."
  "2026-10-26T22:06:35.538Z",codex-agent,"The npm gate stopped emitting results after its interrupted-before-dispatch namespace test failed. Read-only process inspection found the decision-recovery worker idle (zero CPU ticks during a two-second sample), no children, and one listening socket after all file cases had reported. The HTTP fixture starts its server before awaiting workspace initialization, outside the cleanup try/finally, so an initialization failure can retain a listener. Only that owned idle test worker was terminated to let the already-failed gate collect remaining results; this run is unaccepted and must not be counted as a complete passing gate. No production process, test assertion, timeout or source code was changed. Bun passed the two non-timeout recovery cases. The detailed npm failure causes still need the runner final report."
  "2026-10-26T23:01:37.330Z",codex-agent,"Stopped npm diagnostic receipt: after the original 300000 ms crash-drill timeout, received-headers recovery failed with ENOENT while the SDK runtime bridge restored a previous fixture working directory that had been removed; interrupted-before-dispatch then failed with uv_cwd. The packed LM CLI child separately exceeded its unchanged 20-second bound. The idle receipt-recovery worker had one leaked listener and required termination. The already-unaccepted npm gate was later ended with SIGINT to flush its buffered errors while Bun and all three exact-head CI jobs continued. Reported partial totals are 554 collected tests: 530 pass, 3 fail, 21 cancelled, zero skips; this is not the complete expected 1026-case gate or an accepted pass. Both non-timeout receipt cases pass in the full Bun run and the headers case passes in isolation. These observations do not establish a separate SDK regression without a controlled baseline. The original lineage regressions pass in both runs with unchanged assertions."
  "2026-10-26T23:06:58.631Z",codex-agent,"Final local Bun diagnostic was intentionally ended after the unchanged 300000 ms HTTP crash-drill timeout had already made the gate unaccepted. Reported partial totals: 600 collected tests, 581 pass, zero assertion failures, 19 cancellations including the deadline and interrupted remaining files, zero skips; exit 1. This is not a complete 1026-case run or an accepted gate. The npm diagnostic also exited 1 with the partial totals and removed-fixture cwd cascade recorded above. Both originally failing lineage cases pass in both runtimes, and the isolated headers recovery passes. All non-coverage release stages passed in the clean publication worktree. Full exact-head CI is the remaining validation; report its outcome separately. No tests were skipped in source, no assertion, threshold or deadline was changed, and no claim of local full-gate success is made."
  "2026-11-02T09:58:36.780Z",codex-sol,"Reobserved during the complete SDK 2026.11.2 Node 26 release gate: SIGKILL at every HTTP-to-PM receipt boundary replays one decision per query reached its unchanged 300000 ms timeout (reported 300001.667725 ms). No behavioral assertion failure has been reported for this case. The complete suite is continuing; its final counts and coverage gate remain unaccepted until collected. All three SDK-specific regressions pass focused verification. Reusing this existing timing follow-up; no timeout, assertion or coverage threshold is changed."
  "2026-11-02T10:25:34.209Z",codex-sol,"The same complete instrumented run also reobserved the packed LM CLI 20-second child bound, previously noted on this item: packed pm CLI performs three real LM generations and records contamination refusal under 20 seconds reported failure at 27073.038069 ms. Detailed runner errors will be collected at full completion. No deadline, behavioral assertion or source scope has been changed. Independent verification of both timing cases is pending after the full suite."
  "2026-11-02T12:11:10.058Z",codex-sol,"Completed full Node 26 gate: 1474 tests, 1472 pass, 1 failure (packed CLI real CLI took 22948 ms against 20000 ms), 1 cancellation (receipt crash drill 300000 ms deadline), 0 skipped. All 58 source files were measured at 100 percent in all four dimensions using the unchanged gate helpers, but the test gate exited 1. Independent packed CLI re-run under coverage also failed its existing assertion at 22645 ms; its 25000 ms subprocess watchdog did not cause that assertion. Independent receipt crash verification is running. Keeping all existing bounds and assertions; no causal performance attribution is made yet."
  "2026-11-02T12:17:15.436Z",codex-sol,"Independent receipt crash drill passed all eight scenarios under the unchanged 300000 ms deadline: 186641.946885 ms, 1/1, zero skips/cancellations. Independent packed CLI remains over its unchanged 20000 ms assertion at 22645 ms. A detached green 4d98fdb baseline, built separately with actual SDK 2026.10.27 module resolution, also fails the identical CLI assertion at 23693 ms (1 test, zero skips). This establishes pre-upgrade reproducibility of that timing failure on this host, not a controlled SDK speed comparison. The full 1474-case gate remains unaccepted for the two recorded timing cases; all thresholds, timeouts and behavioral assertions remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-02T20:50:45.058Z",pi-glm,"New round: CI 41444134492 shows packed CLI tests 2-4x slower on feat/predeclared-sequential-evaluation (deaabf9) vs main (Node 26: 51.0s/61.7s vs 13.5s/14.6s; Node 22: 25.2s/25.0s vs 16.2s/14.2s; job 5629s vs 2711s). Plan: interleaved A/B timing on branch vs main, per-step instrumentation (pm invocations, SDK reads/writes, history scans, fsync, spawns), root-cause fix, regression guard, revert proof."
  "2026-11-02T21:41:49.587Z",pi-glm,"Root cause found for the packed-CLI slowdown (CI 41444134292, Node 26 ETIMEDOUTs; Node 22 2x). Method: interleaved A/B on the same host (packed-loop harness + the two packed tests), SDK chunk stack tracing, strace execve counts, per-SDK-method timing instrumentation, and node --cpu-prof.\n\nROOT CAUSE: commit a033367 moved ensurePersistentTypes into createRlItem, so every created item re-issued all 9 schemaAddType SDK calls. Each schemaAddType re-resolves the merge-attribute workspace and spawns 'git rev-parse --show-toplevel' (PATH-scanned: 2700 execve attempts for 225 invocations in one 3-generation loop; main does 45). One packed lm loop: 25 creates x 9 types = 225 git spawns; the loop test fixture loop: 243 schemaAddType calls through one client. Each invocation costs ~40-50ms on CI runners, which dominates the packed-CLI wall time (per-SDK-method timing measured schemaAddType at 48ms/call; gets ~12-17ms are fs-latency-bound and unchanged in nature).\n\nFIX: index.ts ensurePersistentTypes now memoizes one completed installation per PmClient in-process (WeakSet). schemaAddType stays byte-idempotent, a fresh process/client/faulted installation still re-runs the full sequence, and every create is still preceded by an installed schema. All durability, drift and refusal guarantees retained; no timeout raised, no assertion weakened, nothing skipped."
  "2026-11-02T21:41:54.939Z",pi-glm,"A/B evidence, interleaved pairs on the same host (packed 3-generation lm loop, harness-measured ms; full packed tests in parentheses).\n\nBEFORE (branch pre-fix vs main):\n- lm loop, node 24: branch 30911/27949/27527 vs main 21865/19534/18016 (branch mean ~28.8s vs main ~19.8s, +45%).\n- lm loop, node 26: branch 23212/21662/18822 vs main 15454/14307/13368 (+47%).\n- packed lm test: branch failed the <20s assertion (21.3-23.2s measured); packed process test failed all 3 rounds at the unchanged 20s subprocess timeout (branch wall 30.2-30.3s) while main passed at 13.8-17.7s measured.\n- spawn counts per lm loop: branch 225 git invocations (2700 execve attempts) + 12 getconf; main 45 (540).\n\nAFTER (branch fixed vs main):\n- lm loop, node 24: branch 19950/20920/20038 vs main 19733/17309/20623 (+6%, within host noise).\n- lm loop, node 26: branch 20745/16380/15936 vs main 17512/15712/15131 (~+10% mean, residual is the branch's added drift-verification reads which are kept by design).\n- packed lm test: passes, 16569/16761 ms vs the unchanged 20-second assertion.\n- packed process test: passes all 3 rounds, 16431/17116/15085 ms measured vs main 13269/14279/16832.\n- spawn counts per lm loop: branch 9 git invocations (108 execve attempts), below main's 45.\n\nRemaining ~5-10% gap vs main comes from the branch's additional drift-verification SDK reads (543 gets vs 360, 372 config reads vs 140) which are part of the added guarantees and are fs-latency-bound, not process spawns."
  "2026-11-02T21:41:59.017Z",pi-glm,"REGRESSION GUARD + revert proof: test/loop.test.ts now runs one full promoted loop through a counting client and asserts schemaAddType stays <= 2 x RL_ITEM_TYPES.length (18) per client, and > 0 so the first-create installation cannot be dropped. With the fix: pass (9 calls). With the fix reverted: FAIL, 'one loop made 243 schemaAddType calls through one client' (27 creates x 9 types). Revert proof recorded; bound cannot pass at the reverted 243."
  "2026-11-03T03:39:09.614Z",orchestrator,"Orchestrator verification (2026-11-03): the agent hit its 6-hour limit inside the full npm release gate before committing. I reviewed the diff: the per-client WeakSet memo for ensurePersistentTypes, the schemaAddType budget guard in test/loop.test.ts, and the warm-client boundary measurement in test/training-influence.test.ts, which the memo makes necessary. Typecheck and lint pass. node --test test/loop.test.ts test/training-influence.test.ts: one failure on the first run at host load ~25, then a clean re-run with no failures. CI runs the full npm and Bun gates on the pushed head."
